      "ayah_arabic": "كِلۡتَا ٱلۡجَنَّتَيۡنِ ءَاتَتۡ أُكُلَهَا وَلَمۡ تَظۡلِم مِّنۡهُ شَيۡـࣰٔ اۚ وَفَجَّرۡنَا خِلَٰلَهُمَا نَهَرࣰ ا",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "Al-Kahf",
      "literal_gloss": "Each",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "Each of the two gardens produced its fruit and did not fall short thereof in anything. And We caused to gush forth within them a river.",
        "pickthall": "Each of the gardens gave its fruit and withheld naught thereof. And We caused a river to gush forth therein.",
        "khattab": "Each garden yielded ˹all˺ its produce, never falling short. And We caused a river to flow between them",
        "arberry": "each of the two gardens yielded its produce and failed naught in any wise; and We caused to gush amidst them a river."
